1089
00:59:13.654 --> 00:59:15.821
Hamish Hawks doesn't own
Silent Beauty.

1090
00:59:15.823 --> 00:59:16.890
You sure?

1091
00:59:17.425 --> 00:59:18.692
It was on his yacht.

1092
00:59:19.160 --> 00:59:21.528
That's not Hamish's yacht.

1093
00:59:21.595 --> 00:59:23.964
It belongs to one of
his business associates.

1094
00:59:24.031 --> 00:59:25.532
No. no. no.

1095
00:59:25.534 --> 00:59:27.167
That's why Richter's here.

1096
00:59:28.702 --> 00:59:30.337
Hell fucking no.

1097
00:59:31.172 --> 00:59:33.340
Please don't say what I
think you're about to say.

1098
00:59:34.141 --> 00:59:36.809
Salzar owns the painting
and the yacht.

1099
00:59:36.811 --> 00:59:38.010
Is that right?

1100
00:59:38.012 --> 00:59:40.779
Well. technically. the
painting and the yacht

1101
00:59:40.781 --> 00:59:43.949
are listed under a couple
of his shell companies.

1102
00:59:43.951 --> 00:59:45.317
But yeah. Mason. you're right.

1103
00:59:45.319 --> 00:59:46.520
It's Salsar.

1104
00:59:47.288 --> 00:59:49.423
How can you be so sure?

1105
00:59:49.558 --> 00:59:54.161
Because I'm the one
that brokered the deal back
when he bought the painting.

1106
00:59:56.163 --> 01:00:00.334
Abel Salzar is my client.

1107
01:00:01.469 --> 01:00:02.000
Oh.

1108
01:00:02.002 --> 01:00:02.668
Oh. shit.

1109
01:00:02.670 --> 01:00:04.371
Oh. hell no.

1110
01:00:11.345 --> 01:00:12.644
Can I try some?

1111
01:00:12.646 --> 01:00:13.345
No.

1112
01:00:13.347 --> 01:00:14.913
You have your own ice cream.

1113
01:00:14.915 --> 01:00:16.249
Whatever.

1114
01:00:19.820 --> 01:00:21.588
What's the matter.
Agent Richter?

1115
01:00:22.389 --> 01:00:23.924
No ice cream for you?

1116
01:00:24.559 --> 01:00:26.259
I'm lactose intolerant.

1117
01:00:27.895 --> 01:00:30.197
You don't seem surprised
to see me.

1118
01:00:30.431 --> 01:00:33.567
You don't really
think I thought
that you were killed
in an explosion.

1119
01:00:33.734 --> 01:00:35.402
You played that trick before.

1120
01:00:35.703 --> 01:00:37.604
Well. this one's not on me. man.

1121
01:00:38.339 --> 01:00:41.375
Maybe it was Decker trying
to put you out of your misery.

1122
01:00:42.109 --> 01:00:44.109
I tell you. I'm sorry to
hear the two of you broke

1123
01:00:44.111 --> 01:00:46.446
up. but I could have
told you a long time ago.

1124
01:00:46.615 --> 01:00:48.082
It was never gonna last.

1125
01:00:48.115 --> 01:00:49.516
Well. you didn't.

1126
01:00:49.618 --> 01:00:51.718
I'm always the last to know.
aren't I?

1127
01:00:51.952 --> 01:00:53.587
You think maybe I have a chance
with her?

1128
01:00:55.122 --> 01:00:58.126
You love to see me in
a tight spot. don't you?

1129
01:00:58.859 --> 01:01:00.894
I'd say I'm entitled
to gloat a little.

1130
01:01:00.928 --> 01:01:03.296
How many times have I
had to chase you in the past?

1131
01:01:03.632 --> 01:01:04.897
Now you're coming to me.

1132
01:01:04.899 --> 01:01:08.033
I would have appreciated
a heads-up once also.

1133
01:01:08.035 --> 01:01:09.770
Now. why would I do that?

1134
01:01:09.904 --> 01:01:12.205
I can just trail
your crew instead.

1135
01:01:12.574 --> 01:01:15.809
Oh. so you admit it.
that you use us as bait.

1136
01:01:16.243 --> 01:01:18.378
I admit to being good
at what I do.

1137
01:01:21.882 --> 01:01:22.983
So where is he?

1138
01:01:23.317 --> 01:01:24.484
Where's Salzar?

1139
01:01:28.889 --> 01:01:29.522
Hm?

1140
01:01:29.524 --> 01:01:30.590
You don't know. do you?

1141
01:01:31.892 --> 01:01:33.192
Oh. my god.

1142
01:01:33.194 --> 01:01:35.829
You almost get us killed. and
you don't even know where he is.

1143
01:01:36.430 --> 01:01:38.397
Maybe you're not as
good as you say you are.

1144
01:01:38.399 --> 01:01:39.765
Yeah. well. he's not an idiot.

1145
01:01:39.767 --> 01:01:41.334
And I know he's
around here somewhere.

1146
01:01:41.670 --> 01:01:43.670
But he uses proxies
for everything.

1147
01:01:43.672 --> 01:01:45.470
His proxies have proxies.

1148
01:01:45.472 --> 01:01:46.840
The man's a ghost.

1149
01:01:47.576 --> 01:01:49.509
And now he thinks I'm a ghost.
so.

1150
01:01:49.511 --> 01:01:50.809
Well. lucky for you.

1151
01:01:50.811 --> 01:01:52.679
No. unlucky for him.

1152
01:01:52.681 --> 01:01:54.082
I'm tired of this shit.

1153
01:01:55.282 --> 01:01:56.516
We've gotten him before.

1154
01:01:56.518 --> 01:01:57.684
We'll get him again.

1155
01:01:57.818 --> 01:01:58.518
What are you saying?

1156
01:01:58.520 --> 01:01:59.686
You have a plan?

1157
01:01:59.688 --> 01:02:00.654
I do.

1158
01:02:01.989 --> 01:02:03.024
I think I do.

1159
01:02:03.924 --> 01:02:05.159
Tell me more.

1160
01:02:31.285 --> 01:02:34.621
I think that was the best
pasta I've ever tasted.

1161
01:02:34.855 --> 01:02:35.320
No. really

1162
01:02:35.322 --> 01:02:36.989
Well. thank you.

1163
01:02:36.991 --> 01:02:38.824
How do you do that?

1164
01:02:38.826 --> 01:02:43.295
Well. actually.
I used to go out
with one of the biggest chefs
in the world.

1165
01:02:43.297 --> 01:02:44.564
You've seen him on TV.

1166
01:02:44.566 --> 01:02:47.032
And I picked up a few skills.

1167
01:02:47.034 --> 01:02:47.766
That makes sense.

1168
01:02:47.768 --> 01:02:50.837
Before. I caught him in bed with

1169
01:02:51.171 --> 01:02:53.706
an Academy Award
winning actress.

1170
01:02:53.708 --> 01:02:54.841
I'm sorry.

1171
01:02:56.844 --> 01:02:58.143
Don't be.

1172
01:02:58.145 --> 01:03:02.582
I'm enjoying taking time just
for myself.

1173
01:03:03.518 --> 01:03:05.017
You know?

1174
01:03:05.019 --> 01:03:08.722
It can get lonely. but everybody
gets a little lonely sometimes.

1175
01:03:09.857 --> 01:03:12.392
Probably even someone
like Abel Salazar.

1176
01:03:14.228 --> 01:03:16.429
How long have you been working
with him?

1177
01:03:16.598 --> 01:03:21.501
Well. his people used
to buy some of
the art I stole back
when I was a thief.

1178
01:03:22.236 --> 01:03:25.437
And once I went legit. I did
some business with Hamish.

1179
01:03:25.439 --> 01:03:28.708
but then I realized that
Hamish was just the middleman.

1180
01:03:28.710 --> 01:03:30.409
Salazar was the real buyer.

1181
01:03:30.411 --> 01:03:35.548
Eventually.
Abel came to trust
me enough to work
with me directly.

1182
01:03:35.550 --> 01:03:38.752
You should be careful with him.

1183
01:03:39.788 --> 01:03:45.525
I know he's suave
and sophisticated
and all that.
but he's a bad man.

1184
01:03:46.093 --> 01:03:47.694
I can take care of myself.

1185
01:03:47.696 --> 01:03:49.094
I know you can.

1186
01:03:49.096 --> 01:03:51.531
I just wouldn't want
to see anything happen
to you. that's all.

1187
01:03:52.701 --> 01:03:53.700
Why?

1188
01:03:54.769 --> 01:03:55.869
Because I care.

1189
01:03:56.403 --> 01:03:57.571
I care about you.

1190
01:04:00.608 --> 01:04:01.975
Mason.

1191
01:04:02.711 --> 01:04:04.878
We should talk more
about this plan.

1192
01:04:06.113 --> 01:04:07.245
The plan. Mason?

1193
01:04:07.247 --> 01:04:09.314
We've gone
over it half a dozen times.

1194
01:04:09.316 --> 01:04:12.217
Yeah. but we don't have a
plan B. and that's important.

1195
01:04:12.219 --> 01:04:16.455
With a plan A that's good.
you don't need a plan B.
I don't know about that.

1196
01:04:16.457 --> 01:04:19.459
Mason. we've got this.

1197
01:04:21.428 --> 01:04:24.898
Okay. well.
I should go check on the crew.

1198
01:04:25.966 --> 01:04:28.902
Make sure
that Sean doesn't get
in trouble.

1199
01:04:30.237 --> 01:04:31.436
He's lucky to have you.

1200
01:04:31.438 --> 01:04:32.706
They all are.

1201
01:04:33.107 --> 01:04:34.841
I feel the same way about them.

1202
01:04:35.342 --> 01:04:37.777
You know. they drive me a
little crazy. but I feel happy.

1203
01:04:37.779 --> 01:04:38.578
Family.

1204
01:04:38.580 --> 01:04:39.512
Family.

1205
01:04:40.080 --> 01:04:40.947
Good night.

1206
01:04:45.419 --> 01:04:46.453
Good night. Mace.

1207
01:04:46.654 --> 01:04:47.754
French way.

1208
01:04:56.163 --> 01:04:57.131
Oh. my God.

1209
01:04:57.331 --> 01:04:58.029
So decadent.

1210
01:04:58.031 --> 01:04:59.133
I love it.

1211
01:04:59.266 --> 01:05:00.298
You finish it.

1212
01:05:00.300 --> 01:05:01.366
I'm stuffed.

1213
01:05:01.368 --> 01:05:03.770
Oh. are you sure I'm not
getting too much sugar?

1214
01:05:04.438 --> 01:05:06.706
That was a pretty good line.
huh?

1215
01:05:06.875 --> 01:05:09.176
You're very convincing baby.

1216
01:05:09.511 --> 01:05:11.212
It's what I do.

1217
01:05:11.311 --> 01:05:14.282
I knew he didn't like
bullies. so I played the bully.

1218
01:05:15.115 --> 01:05:18.219
It gave him a little
bit more incentive
to want to steal from me.

1219
01:05:19.153 --> 01:05:21.621
Or at least to think it was
you he was stealing from.

1220
01:05:21.623 --> 01:05:23.024
That's right.

1221
01:05:23.290 --> 01:05:25.326
I knew he wouldn't be able
to resist.

1222
01:05:26.226 --> 01:05:29.829
Well. you are irresistible.

1223
01:05:30.532 --> 01:05:32.632
Even more so than this cake.

1224
01:05:52.252 --> 01:05:52.984
Hey.

1225
01:05:52.986 --> 01:05:53.987
Hey.

1226
01:05:54.087 --> 01:05:54.821
How was dinner?

1227
01:05:54.823 --> 01:05:56.489
It was good.

1228
01:05:56.658 --> 01:05:59.260
Yeah. I told Odessa it was
the best pasta I ever had.

1229
01:05:59.561 --> 01:06:05.263
Some sort of. like.
lobster. scallops. and.
like. a fettuccine type.

1230
01:06:05.265 --> 01:06:06.334
It was good.

1231
01:06:10.170 --> 01:06:12.340
You know. she still likes you.

1232
01:06:14.274 --> 01:06:16.542
She didn't invite any of
the rest of us to dinner.

1233
01:06:16.544 --> 01:06:18.578
Well.
that's
because we had to make a plan.

1234
01:06:19.179 --> 01:06:20.847
Sure. the plan.

1235
01:06:20.949 --> 01:06:21.948
Mm-hmm.

1236
01:06:23.585 --> 01:06:24.784
Do you trust her?

1237
01:06:28.556 --> 01:06:29.287
Yeah.

1238
01:06:29.289 --> 01:06:30.191
Yeah. I do.

1239
01:06:31.726 --> 01:06:32.625
Good.

1240
01:06:36.363 --> 01:06:39.033
You know. it's... it's okay.

1241
01:06:39.701 --> 01:06:41.868
What's okay?

1242
01:06:41.870 --> 01:06:49.043
I mean. not to sound cheesy
about it. but. like.
it's okay
to open your heart back up.

1243
01:06:52.379 --> 01:06:52.879
Uh...

1244
01:06:52.881 --> 01:06:54.315
My sweet brother.

1245
01:06:54.983 --> 01:06:55.882
Wow.

1246
01:06:55.884 --> 01:06:57.084
You're a good man.

1247
01:06:57.886 --> 01:06:59.420
So are you. Mason.

1248
01:07:00.622 --> 01:07:01.455
Yeah.

1249
01:07:04.759 --> 01:07:06.494
It's getting cold out here.

1250
01:07:07.427 --> 01:07:09.030
You come back inside?

1251
01:07:09.631 --> 01:07:12.665
No. I'm
gonna wait till
the roaches vacate.

1252
01:07:12.967 --> 01:07:14.266
Then I'll go back in.

1253
01:07:14.268 --> 01:07:17.171
Yeah. this is definitely a step
down from that resort. huh?

1254
01:07:26.446 --> 01:07:29.183
Odessa. how did the auction go?

1255
01:07:29.751 --> 01:07:30.616
Excellent.

1256
01:07:30.618 --> 01:07:33.187
I got you every piece
you wanted.

1257
01:07:34.022 --> 01:07:35.320
Of course you did.

1258
01:07:35.322 --> 01:07:37.091
That's why I pay you so well.

1259
01:07:37.525 --> 01:07:39.959
I'll have them all
delivered to you tomorrow.

1260
01:07:40.028 --> 01:07:44.331
And I was thinking
I might make the drive up
and see you and Hector as well.

1261
01:07:45.098 --> 01:07:47.700
Oh. and to what would we owe
that honor?

1262
01:07:48.201 --> 01:07:50.037
I have a surprise for you.

1263
01:07:50.872 --> 01:07:52.470
What is it with women
and surprises?

1264
01:07:52.472 --> 01:07:55.942
It's about Mason Goddard.

1265
01:07:56.044 --> 01:07:57.442
Yes. I know.

1266
01:07:57.444 --> 01:07:59.011
Mason Goddard. he's dead.

1267
01:07:59.013 --> 01:08:00.214
He's fish food.

1268
01:08:01.315 --> 01:08:02.314
No. Abel.

1269
01:08:02.316 --> 01:08:04.118
Mason is alive.

1270
01:08:04.786 --> 01:08:07.288
And he's
going to make a move
against you.

1271
01:08:08.455 --> 01:08:11.858
And I know exactly
what he's planning to do.

1272
01:08:28.208 --> 01:08:29.742
Please open your trunk. ma'am.

1273
01:08:29.811 --> 01:08:30.643
Sure.

1274
01:08:39.988 --> 01:08:40.987
We're clear.

1275
01:08:44.726 --> 01:08:45.859
Welcome. ma'am.

1276
01:08:45.927 --> 01:08:47.225
Thank you.

1277
01:08:47.227 --> 01:08:49.662
The truck with
the new
artwork will be following
shortly.

1278
01:08:50.397 --> 01:08:51.532
All right. thanks.

1279
01:09:14.421 --> 01:09:16.555
I'm going to have to frisk you.

1280
01:09:16.557 --> 01:09:18.524
Well. have at it. handsome.

1281
01:09:18.526 --> 01:09:21.095
Although I don't know
where I'd be hiding anything.

1282
01:09:21.294 --> 01:09:23.261
That won't be necessary.

1283
01:09:23.263 --> 01:09:27.301
Odessa will never hurt me.
because that would be very bad
for business.

1284
01:09:29.137 --> 01:09:31.103
I might try to steal from you.

1285
01:09:31.105 --> 01:09:32.538
Oh. my god.

1286
01:09:32.540 --> 01:09:35.576
Your commissions
on these deals
are already grand larceny.
my dear.

1287
01:09:35.777 --> 01:09:37.743
You know I'm worth it.

1288
01:09:37.745 --> 01:09:39.580
Oh. you definitely are.

1289
01:09:40.213 --> 01:09:42.715
So you noticed the new
landscaping. right?

1290
01:09:42.717 --> 01:09:44.482
Well. yeah.
I did. You have like..

1291
01:09:44.484 --> 01:09:45.751
A park in front of your house.

1292
01:09:45.753 --> 01:09:46.719
It's beautiful. right?

1293
01:09:46.721 --> 01:09:47.820
Yeah.

1294
01:09:48.556 --> 01:09:50.124
So. what do you think?

1295
01:09:51.592 --> 01:09:54.392
Oh.
cute little place you got here.
Abel.

1296
01:09:54.394 --> 01:09:55.629
My humble abode.

1297
01:09:56.296 --> 01:09:57.328
Where's the restroom?

1298
01:09:57.330 --> 01:09:59.233
Right down the hall on the left.

1299
01:09:59.266 --> 01:10:00.132
Thank you.

1300
01:10:00.134 --> 01:10:01.332
I'll wait
for you in the brain room.

1301
01:10:01.334 --> 01:10:02.069
All right.

1302
01:10:07.240 --> 01:10:14.181
Bold move to
so prominently display
a supposedly destroyed work
of art. Abel.

1303
01:10:18.485 --> 01:10:20.287
Your collection has grown.

1304
01:10:20.487 --> 01:10:21.355
Yeah.

1305
01:10:24.025 --> 01:10:25.259
Interesting.

1306
01:10:26.326 --> 01:10:28.195
That is Alex.

1307
01:10:30.164 --> 01:10:32.466
You name your guns?

1308
01:10:33.134 --> 01:10:35.636
Well.
that one has a special meaning
to me.

1309
01:10:36.671 --> 01:10:38.672
You consider this a piece
of art?

1310
01:10:39.040 --> 01:10:40.641
Why not?

1311
01:10:42.143 --> 01:10:45.646
But don't touch it.
because that is a real gun.

1312
01:10:48.381 --> 01:10:49.717
Is it loaded?

1313
01:10:51.485 --> 01:10:52.986
Of course it is.

1314
01:10:53.888 --> 01:10:56.789
An unloaded weapon
is like a blank canvas.

1315
01:10:56.991 --> 01:11:01.228
Useful to the artist. but of
no use to a collector like me.

1316
01:11:02.295 --> 01:11:03.629
Can I offer you champagne?

1317
01:11:03.631 --> 01:11:05.633
Well. I never say no to bubbly.

1318
01:11:06.466 --> 01:11:09.169
Nectar. Odessa is here.

1319
01:11:16.309 --> 01:11:17.877
Odessa.

1320
01:11:17.879 --> 01:11:18.343
Hello.

1321
01:11:18.345 --> 01:11:19.410
Love the outfit.

1322
01:11:19.412 --> 01:11:21.479
Oh. right back at you.

1323
01:11:21.481 --> 01:11:22.581
So good to see you.

1324
01:11:22.583 --> 01:11:23.082
Yeah?

1325
01:11:23.084 --> 01:11:23.516
You look amazing.

1326
01:11:23.518 --> 01:11:24.650
How are you?

1327
01:11:24.652 --> 01:11:25.918
Everything's wonderful.

1328
01:11:25.920 --> 01:11:26.752
Good.

1329
01:11:26.754 --> 01:11:29.021
So happy we... I know.
we did it.

1330
01:11:29.023 --> 01:11:31.158
Sweetheart. right on time.

1331
01:11:32.160 --> 01:11:34.495
So. what are we celebrating?

1332
01:11:34.829 --> 01:11:37.428
Well. to fine art.

1333
01:11:37.430 --> 01:11:39.198
I like that.

1334
01:11:39.200 --> 01:11:42.036
Here's to owning
art the whole world
thinks has been lost.

1335
01:11:42.537 --> 01:11:44.003
How about...

1336
01:11:44.539 --> 01:11:47.574
to owning the entire world.

1337
01:11:48.910 --> 01:11:50.444
Salud.

1338
01:11:50.545 --> 01:11:51.345
Cheers.

1339
01:14:19.994 --> 01:14:21.562
We've been expecting you.

1340
01:14:28.202 --> 01:14:29.001
Clear!

1341
01:15:25.092 --> 01:15:27.060
Sean got
caught
before I could pick him up.

1342
01:15:28.162 --> 01:15:29.329
Damn it.

1343
01:15:36.737 --> 01:15:38.071
Be careful. babe.

1344
01:15:49.950 --> 01:15:53.687
Gentlemen. please
unload the crates over here.

1345
01:15:55.089 --> 01:15:56.957
And give them a hand. please.

1346
01:16:04.298 --> 01:16:06.099
Right over here. please.

1347
01:16:08.102 --> 01:16:09.770
This is exciting.

1348
01:16:19.780 --> 01:16:22.149
A gift from me to you. Abel.

1349
01:16:22.517 --> 01:16:24.349
Abel does not like surprises.

1350
01:16:24.351 --> 01:16:26.718
Well. this is no surprise.
Nectar.

1351
01:16:26.720 --> 01:16:28.989
Odessa gave me
a heads-up last night.

1352
01:16:29.023 --> 01:16:29.822
Oh?

1353
01:16:29.824 --> 01:16:30.724
What is it?

1354
01:16:30.858 --> 01:16:31.858
Open it!

1355
01:16:43.204 --> 01:16:44.905
Bravo!

1356
01:16:46.140 --> 01:16:50.811
Just like Lazarus. Mason
God arises from the dead.

1357
01:16:52.413 --> 01:16:53.580
How?

1358
01:16:53.582 --> 01:16:56.883
Well. vermin are notoriously
difficult to exterminate.

1359
01:16:56.984 --> 01:16:59.384
Yeah.
it can be hard to kill a rat.

1360
01:16:59.386 --> 01:17:00.752
Mm-hmm.

1361
01:17:00.754 --> 01:17:03.423
Well.
maybe this was meant
to be. baby.

1362
01:17:03.891 --> 01:17:06.060
You regretted Mason
didn't suffer more?

1363
01:17:06.227 --> 01:17:07.560
Well. that's right.

1364
01:17:07.562 --> 01:17:09.563
Now we have the chance
to fix that.

1365
01:17:10.231 --> 01:17:12.199
You know.
Mason and I go way back.

1366
01:17:12.534 --> 01:17:16.435
We once even competed to steal
the same Giacometti sculpture.

1367
01:17:16.437 --> 01:17:18.271
And he won that little game.

1368
01:17:18.339 --> 01:17:21.241
But now I win
a much bigger game.

1369
01:17:22.176 --> 01:17:23.610
Really?

1370
01:17:24.211 --> 01:17:26.413
I was just a game to you. huh.
Odessa?

1371
01:17:27.848 --> 01:17:31.284
He thought that I would
help him steal from you.

1372
01:17:31.418 --> 01:17:32.519
Oh.

1373
01:17:32.554 --> 01:17:34.052
So what was the plan?

1374
01:17:34.054 --> 01:17:36.589
Sneak into my villa. make
away with some of my

1375
01:17:36.591 --> 01:17:39.626
valuables. and what.
drive off into the sunset?

1376
01:17:40.961 --> 01:17:44.398
Well. when you say it like that.
it sounds pretty simple. but...

1377
01:17:44.899 --> 01:17:47.567
Yeah. I guess that was the plan.

1378
01:17:48.537 --> 01:17:49.536
You trust her?

1379
01:17:51.472 --> 01:17:52.704
Thanks. Odessa.

1380
01:17:52.706 --> 01:17:54.508
Best gift ever.

1381
01:17:55.142 --> 01:17:58.210
Well. to be fair. it is a gift I
expect to be compensated for.

1382
01:17:58.212 --> 01:18:00.614
Oh. you will be. I promise.

1383
01:18:01.616 --> 01:18:06.154
Just curious. Odessa. how
much is my life worth to you?

1384
01:18:06.420 --> 01:18:07.988
What's the number?

1385
01:18:09.957 --> 01:18:11.992
Probably not as
much as you think.

1386
01:18:15.829 --> 01:18:20.600
Did you really think
I was going
to let you rip
off my biggest client?

1387
01:18:20.768 --> 01:18:23.737
Because once upon a time. you
used to mean something to me.

1388
01:18:24.673 --> 01:18:25.972
Yeah. I guess I did.

1389
01:18:30.177 --> 01:18:32.779
First Decker. now this.

1390
01:18:33.180 --> 01:18:35.582
You have terrible luck
with women. Mason.

1391
01:18:36.450 --> 01:18:37.818
Maybe I do.

1392
01:18:37.985 --> 01:18:40.587
And I almost feel sorry for you.

1393
01:18:42.591 --> 01:18:43.890
I guess it's a...

1394
01:18:45.527 --> 01:18:48.995
There's always plan B.
- Plan B?

1395
01:18:56.503 --> 01:18:57.637
Where is he?

1396
01:18:57.706 --> 01:18:59.104
No. no. no. no. no. no.

1397
01:18:59.106 --> 01:19:00.440
Go find him!

1398
01:22:07.562 --> 01:22:08.662
You ready. babe?

1399
01:22:08.730 --> 01:22:10.031
On your word. honey.

1400
01:22:24.913 --> 01:22:25.912
Now!

1401
01:22:26.180 --> 01:22:27.714
Fire in the hole.

1402
01:22:46.233 --> 01:22:47.600
Son of a bitch.

1403
01:22:48.235 --> 01:22:48.734
It's okay. baby.

1404
01:22:48.736 --> 01:22:49.468
Hey. it's okay.

1405
01:22:49.470 --> 01:22:50.870
Somebody's gonna pay for this.

1406
01:22:51.071 --> 01:22:51.904
It's okay.

1407
01:22:51.906 --> 01:22:53.007
It's okay.

1408
01:22:55.777 --> 01:22:56.609
Move.

1409
01:22:56.945 --> 01:22:57.911
Move?

1410
01:22:58.580 --> 01:22:59.447
Jeez.

1411
01:23:02.851 --> 01:23:04.750
You need to chill out. bro.

1412
01:23:04.752 --> 01:23:07.221
Maybe you should try
some CBD gummies.

1413
01:23:07.421 --> 01:23:11.058
Maybe you should stay off
yachts where you're not welcome.

1414
01:23:15.028 --> 01:23:16.896
What the fuck. Odessa?

1415
01:23:16.898 --> 01:23:18.363
Hey. I did my part.

1416
01:23:18.365 --> 01:23:19.397
I delivered him to you.

1417
01:23:19.399 --> 01:23:21.268
I'm not the one
who let him get away.

1418
01:23:21.368 --> 01:23:23.034
You can always get
another yacht. baby.

1419
01:23:23.036 --> 01:23:25.072
Maybe even a bigger one.

1420
01:23:25.372 --> 01:23:28.242
Hey. this is the guy
who blew up your yacht.

1421
01:23:32.145 --> 01:23:33.381
Where's Mason?

1422
01:23:33.748 --> 01:23:34.614
I don't know. sir.

1423
01:23:34.616 --> 01:23:36.050
Then go find him!

1424
01:23:42.256 --> 01:23:44.758
Why
the fuck would you blow
up my yacht?

1425
01:23:45.727 --> 01:23:47.261
Oh. my God.

1426
01:23:48.763 --> 01:23:50.563
You still
haven't figured it out.
have you?

1427
01:23:50.565 --> 01:23:51.931
Hands up now?

1428
01:23:55.068 --> 01:23:56.070
You got me.

1429
01:23:56.470 --> 01:23:57.304
Weapon.

1430
01:24:04.244 --> 01:24:05.678
Why would you come back?

1431
01:24:05.680 --> 01:24:07.680
I thought your brother
was the dumb one.

1432
01:24:08.783 --> 01:24:11.085
My brother's a lot of
things. but he's not dumb.

1433
01:24:11.986 --> 01:24:12.952
You know what?

1434
01:24:12.954 --> 01:24:14.522
Thank you. Mason.

1435
01:24:14.622 --> 01:24:16.989
What is it exactly that I
haven't figured out yet?

1436
01:24:16.991 --> 01:24:19.160
Sean. do the honors.

1437
01:24:20.260 --> 01:24:22.096
You ever heard of 4D chess?

1438
01:24:22.597 --> 01:24:24.365
Oh. Jesus Christ.

1439
01:24:25.098 --> 01:24:27.435
Mason wasn't the only one
in those crates.

1440
01:24:37.011 --> 01:24:40.481
So Anton and the new
guy are here somewhere.

1441
01:24:40.782 --> 01:24:42.113
Perfect.

1442
01:24:42.115 --> 01:24:45.785
Manme will find them.
and you can all die together.

1443
01:24:49.691 --> 01:24:50.523
Sweet Link.

1444
01:24:50.525 --> 01:24:51.724
Let's get this shit.

1445
01:24:51.726 --> 01:24:53.693
Hey. hey. you just make
sure you hold on right there.

1446
01:24:53.728 --> 01:24:55.463
Let's get the fuck out
of here now.

1447
01:25:02.369 --> 01:25:03.571
So what?

1448
01:25:07.407 --> 01:25:09.075
So now you steal my car?

1449
01:25:09.077 --> 01:25:10.408
I'm supposed to be impressed.

1450
01:25:10.410 --> 01:25:11.677
They have dozens of them.

1451
01:25:11.679 --> 01:25:15.082
Yeah. well. auto theft.
it's not our strong suit.

1452
01:25:17.384 --> 01:25:18.452
You.

1453
01:25:18.820 --> 01:25:20.087
You're part of this.

1454
01:25:20.555 --> 01:25:21.754
Who. me?

1455
01:25:22.924 --> 01:25:23.790
Yeah.

1456
01:25:24.092 --> 01:25:25.459
Oh. shit.

1457
01:25:25.660 --> 01:25:27.526
I knew I was forgetting
something.

1458
01:25:27.528 --> 01:25:28.426
No. you're doing good.

1459
01:25:28.428 --> 01:25:30.128
You're good.

1460
01:25:30.130 --> 01:25:34.602
I mean.
didn't you wonder how
Mason was able to start
that boat so quickly?

1461
01:25:35.268 --> 01:25:36.869
Hey.
cute little place you got here.
Abel.

1462
01:25:36.871 --> 01:25:38.104
My humble abode.

1463
01:25:38.106 --> 01:25:39.939
Where's the restroom?

1464
01:25:39.941 --> 01:25:41.741
Right down the hall on the left.

1465
01:25:41.776 --> 01:25:42.642
Thank you.

1466
01:25:42.644 --> 01:25:44.010
I'll wait
for you in the break room.

1467
01:25:44.012 --> 01:25:44.744
All right.

1468
01:26:07.135 --> 01:26:08.934
I don't understand boats.
but that does sound like

1469
01:26:08.936 --> 01:26:11.138
something that should
have occurred to you. Abel.

1470
01:26:11.204 --> 01:26:12.303
I'm just saying.

1471
01:26:12.305 --> 01:26:13.739
Yeah. yeah. yeah.

1472
01:26:13.741 --> 01:26:16.410
And while all
that was happening.
I was sneaking out of the yacht.

1473
01:26:16.443 --> 01:26:17.478
All stealthy.

1474
01:26:17.779 --> 01:26:18.945
Like a badass.

1475
01:26:19.446 --> 01:26:21.348
Like a ninja.

1476
01:26:23.316 --> 01:26:26.552
And not that you would
care. Salazar. but don't worry.

1477
01:26:26.554 --> 01:26:29.722
Link made sure
the whole crew
was safe
before we blew up the yacht.

1478
01:26:29.824 --> 01:26:31.256
She made a little
call this morning.

1479
01:26:31.258 --> 01:26:32.490
Yes. Captain.

1480
01:26:32.492 --> 01:26:36.063
This is Suzanne Connors from
Custom Yachts Incorporated.

1481
01:26:36.130 --> 01:26:40.733
I'm afraid we've got
a little problem
with a carbon monoxide leak
on your vessel.

1482
01:26:40.968 --> 01:26:43.604
You need
to evacuate the crew
immediately.

1483
01:26:44.839 --> 01:26:46.640
Yeah. I understand.

1484
01:26:47.942 --> 01:26:51.744
Our technicians are on the
way to fix the issue right now.

1485
01:26:51.746 --> 01:26:54.181
And did you see that explosion?

1486
01:26:55.750 --> 01:27:00.787
It was our best
distraction ever.
giving Mason the chance
to sneak back here.

1487
01:27:05.526 --> 01:27:08.527
and giving me a chance
to finally blow his brains out.

1488
01:27:08.529 --> 01:27:10.631
May I tell you something?

1489
01:27:10.965 --> 01:27:12.497
Now.
I don't know a lot about art.

1490
01:27:12.499 --> 01:27:13.431
I really don't.

1491
01:27:13.433 --> 01:27:16.635
But I really kind
of like this painting.

1492
01:27:16.637 --> 01:27:17.203
Kind of like it?

1493
01:27:17.205 --> 01:27:18.336
Yes.

1494
01:27:18.338 --> 01:27:21.173
It is worth over $100
million. you fucking idiot.

1495
01:27:21.175 --> 01:27:22.875
That's my point. you see.

1496
01:27:23.144 --> 01:27:26.447
But I do know someone
who knows a lot about art.

1497
01:27:26.814 --> 01:27:29.350
And they say. well. they
say that... Ah. ah. ah.

1498
01:27:30.051 --> 01:27:31.685
Back off.

1499
01:27:32.186 --> 01:27:35.353
Okay. let me tell you
from a distance then. okay?

1500
01:27:35.355 --> 01:27:40.526
If you go
to your painting
and you look closely.
okay. you'll see

1501
01:27:40.528 --> 01:27:45.898
that the paint
strokes are perfect.
but they're too perfect. okay?

1502
01:27:45.900 --> 01:27:48.868
There should be little
cracks in the paint stroke.

1503
01:27:48.870 --> 01:27:49.735
Do you see that?

1504
01:27:49.737 --> 01:27:50.636
There's not.

1505
01:27:50.638 --> 01:27:52.206
In the oil paint.

1506
01:27:53.306 --> 01:27:55.643
So I think you've got
a forger on your hands.

1507
01:27:56.844 --> 01:27:58.512
Yeah.

1508
01:27:59.213 --> 01:28:02.515
Oh. and you know. before
Anton and Victor stole your car.

1509
01:28:02.517 --> 01:28:04.184
They swapped the paintings out.

1510
01:28:13.594 --> 01:28:14.593
Sweet Link!

1511
01:28:14.595 --> 01:28:15.227
Hundred mil!

1512
01:28:15.229 --> 01:28:16.497
Whoo!

1513
01:28:19.366 --> 01:28:21.568
Now you all fucking die.

1514
01:28:28.441 --> 01:28:29.610
Uh-oh.

1515
01:28:30.077 --> 01:28:31.345
You know what?

1516
01:28:31.712 --> 01:28:33.681
I know I forgot one last thing.

1517
01:28:34.515 --> 01:28:36.048
Can I offer you champagne?

1518
01:28:36.050 --> 01:28:38.018
Well. I never say no to bubbly.

1519
01:28:38.920 --> 01:28:41.255
Nectar. Odessa is here.

1520
01:28:55.736 --> 01:28:57.237
Motherfucker.

1521
01:29:00.373 --> 01:29:01.240
Checkmate?

1522
01:29:01.242 --> 01:29:01.941
Nope.

1523
01:29:01.943 --> 01:29:02.708
Not quite.

1524
01:29:02.710 --> 01:29:03.610
Almost.

1525
01:29:27.134 --> 01:29:28.067
Hello. Abel.

1526
01:29:28.069 --> 01:29:29.969
It's nice to see you again.

1527
01:29:31.806 --> 01:29:33.474
Why don't you put
that on the floor?

1528
01:29:37.144 --> 01:29:38.011
Now?

1529
01:29:38.079 --> 01:29:39.146
Now.

1530
01:29:39.513 --> 01:29:41.013
Checkmate. Salazar.

1531
01:29:41.015 --> 01:29:44.084
Oh. for fuck's sake. get me
away from these people. please.

1532
01:29:44.451 --> 01:29:45.686
Please!

1533
01:29:58.766 --> 01:30:00.933
So you're like
the mastermind now?

1534
01:30:01.002 --> 01:30:02.803
I can't keep track of you.

1535
01:30:14.447 --> 01:30:18.218
It looks like my old
pal Abel Salazar
is out
of the picture once again.

1536
01:30:18.451 --> 01:30:20.521
Creating quite the power vacuum.

1537
01:30:20.988 --> 01:30:23.856
Sounds like
a business opportunity
for someone like you.

1538
01:30:23.858 --> 01:30:25.692
Opportunity for us.

1539
01:30:27.395 --> 01:30:29.996
You knew he was still alive
this whole time. didn't you?

1540
01:30:30.798 --> 01:30:33.400
Mason. you never said anything
about blowing up the yachts.

1541
01:30:34.535 --> 01:30:36.201
A yacht blew up?

1542
01:30:36.203 --> 01:30:37.002
Yikes.

1543
01:30:37.004 --> 01:30:38.203
Sounds dangerous.

1544
01:30:38.205 --> 01:30:40.374
Yeah. well.
you're lucky nobody got killed.

1545
01:30:40.473 --> 01:30:42.109
Our deal would have been off.

1546
01:30:42.710 --> 01:30:45.579
Why don't you try keeping
him behind bars this time?

1547
01:30:45.746 --> 01:30:47.513
Do I look like a prison warden
to you?

1548
01:30:47.515 --> 01:30:49.249
My job's just to catch him.

1549
01:30:49.817 --> 01:30:51.718
Well then. well done.

1550
01:30:52.219 --> 01:30:53.187
Thanks.

1551
01:30:53.654 --> 01:30:54.787
Do me a favor.

1552
01:30:54.789 --> 01:30:56.322
Keep that brother of
yours out of trouble. please.

1553
01:30:56.324 --> 01:30:57.923
Oh. I can't guarantee that.

1554
01:30:57.925 --> 01:30:59.758
I'd hate to have to put
him behind bars one day.

1555
01:30:59.760 --> 01:31:01.093
You know I will if I have to.

1556
01:31:01.095 --> 01:31:02.296
Hmm.

1557
01:31:02.997 --> 01:31:04.565
But can you keep him there?

1558
01:31:05.199 --> 01:31:06.099
Ah.

1559
01:31:07.101 --> 01:31:08.502
Let's go.

1560
01:31:09.370 --> 01:31:12.039
I never underestimated
Mason Goddard.

1561
01:31:13.207 --> 01:31:15.075
But Abel Salazar sure did.

1562
01:31:16.010 --> 01:31:18.946
You know who else Abel
Salazar underestimated?

1563
01:31:20.448 --> 01:31:21.915
Hamish Hawks.

1564
01:31:23.517 --> 01:31:24.850
Oh. my God.

1565
01:31:24.852 --> 01:31:26.119
Look at this.

1566
01:31:26.187 --> 01:31:28.255
We're almost full of surprises.

1567
01:31:42.203 --> 01:31:43.235
What was that?

1568
01:31:43.237 --> 01:31:44.738
I don't know.

1569
01:31:44.939 --> 01:31:47.873
But
what I do know
is we are something.

1570
01:31:47.875 --> 01:31:49.141
We pulled it off.

1571
01:31:49.143 --> 01:31:49.608
Yeah.

1572
01:31:49.610 --> 01:31:51.210
That was so fun.

1573
01:31:51.212 --> 01:31:52.244
Wasn't it fun?

1574
01:31:52.246 --> 01:31:53.312
Well. yeah.

1575
01:31:53.314 --> 01:31:55.614
I forgot how exciting
the whole thing can be.

1576
01:31:55.616 --> 01:31:58.117
Yeah. well.
you're not thinking
of getting back into the game.
are you?

1577
01:31:58.119 --> 01:31:59.318
No. I don't know about that.

1578
01:31:59.320 --> 01:32:02.721
I might have had enough
excitement for now. at least.

1579
01:32:02.723 --> 01:32:05.057
Well. that's good.
because I need an art expert

1580
01:32:05.059 --> 01:32:07.628
to help me sell that
$100 million painting.

1581
01:32:08.162 --> 01:32:12.731
Oh. my commission is
steep and non-negotiable.

1582
01:32:12.733 --> 01:32:15.302
Yeah. well.
you're gonna earn every penny.

1583
01:32:16.137 --> 01:32:17.736
Did it. guys?

1584
01:32:17.738 --> 01:32:18.737
God. Sean.

1585
01:32:18.739 --> 01:32:20.572
How fucking cool was that?

1586
01:32:20.574 --> 01:32:22.743
It was so cool.

1587
01:32:22.910 --> 01:32:24.478
Oh. man. yeah.

1588
01:32:24.513 --> 01:32:26.345
It's all you. buddy.

1589
01:32:26.347 --> 01:32:32.618
And I have to apologize
for not buying
into this whole 4D chess thing.
and I was wrong.

1590
01:32:32.620 --> 01:32:33.152
Really?

1591
01:32:33.154 --> 01:32:34.386
Yeah. I was wrong.

1592
01:32:34.388 --> 01:32:37.022
Well. that's awesome. man.
because I got this other idea.

1593
01:32:37.024 --> 01:32:38.525
Don't push it.

1594
01:32:38.527 --> 01:32:41.493
No. no. no. I'm
telling you. it's
the greatest idea
for a heist ever.

1595
01:32:41.495 --> 01:32:42.361
Wait. I want to hear it.

1596
01:32:42.363 --> 01:32:43.829
Well. don't encourage him.

1597
01:32:43.831 --> 01:32:44.631
No. I want to hear it.
